   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to making technical corrections to provisions on wildlife",
    "basePrintNo": "S5352",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5352-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §11-0511, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5352\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to making\ntechnical corrections to provisions on wildlife\n\nPURPOSE:\nThe purpose of this bill is to clarify the provision of law\nthat discusses possession and transportation of wildlife.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nThis legislation amends section\n11-0511 of the environmental conservation law, as amended by chapter\n692 of the laws of 2004.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThis legislation clarifies the way in which raccoons\nand reptiles are classified, how they can be possessed, and how they\nmay be transported under the environmental conservation law.\nCurrently, the list of animals that constitute wildlife in this\nsection list include \"venomous reptile or raccoon\". This has been\ninterpreted in various municipalities to mean that a raccoon must be\n\"venomous\" in order to be investigated or removed from an area. A\n\"venomous raccoon\" has been interpreted as an animal with rabies.\nThis is an unnecessary classification for the purposes of this\nsection. This legislation simply moves raccoon to a different part of\nthe list and removes the implied venomous requirement to clarify the\npurpose and intent of this section of law.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
